ENVIRONMENTAL SERVICES IN THE BARANGAY
A. GARBAGE COLLECTION AND SOLID WASTE MANAGEMENT
    Services:

        The barangay provides garbage collection services and promotes proper solid waste management through waste segregation and scheduled garbage collection.

    Steps:
        Barangay officials conduct information dissemination in every Purok to inform residents about:
        Proper waste segregation.
        Garbage collection schedules.
        Designated garbage collection and disposal areas.
        Proper solid waste management practices.
        Residents must properly segregate their garbage and bring it to the designated collection area according to the scheduled garbage collection time.
        The assigned garbage truck collects the segregated garbage from the designated collection area.
        
B. ISSUANCE OF BARANGAY CLEARANCE AS A PREREQUISITE FOR CITY PERMIT TO CUT TREES
    Requirements:
        Request letter.
        Proof of ownership of the property where the tree is located.
        Current Community Tax Certificate (CTC).
        Approval from the Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR) or Community Environment and Natural Resources Office (CENRO).
    Steps:
        Proceed to the Barangay Hall and log in to the record book, stating your purpose to the Officer of the Day.
        Submit the request letter and required documents to the Barangay Secretary for the preparation of the barangay certification.
        The Punong Barangay signs the prepared certification.
        Pay the required fee of ₱100.00 to the Barangay Treasurer.
        Obtain the Official Receipt and claim the issued barangay certification.
        Fees:
        Barangay certification fee: ₱100.00.
        Important Information:
        The barangay certification serves as a prerequisite for applying for a city permit to cut trees.
        The barangay certification is not a substitute for the required city permit or DENR/CENRO approval.